## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where Ollama model discovery could leave non-OK `/api/tags` or `/api/show` response bodies open while falling back to empty discovery results.

## Why This Change Was Made

The discovery fallback behavior is unchanged: failed tag listing still returns an empty reachable model list, and failed show metadata still returns no metadata. Those fallback branches now cancel any response body before returning.

## User Impact

Ollama users keep the same fail-soft model discovery behavior while OpenClaw releases failed discovery response streams promptly.

## Evidence

- Real call chain loopback: `./node_modules/.bin/tsx proof-ollama-provider-models.ts` started a localhost Ollama-style HTTP server, exercised `/api/tags` and `/api/show` 503 fallback responses, and used 200 JSON negative-control responses to verify successful discovery still works.
- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/ollama/src/provider-models.test.ts -- -t "cancels non-OK discovery response bodies|fails soft and stops reading"`
- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/ollama/src/provider-models.test.ts`

```text
$ ./node_modules/.bin/tsx proof-ollama-provider-models.ts
tags-fallback={"reachable":true,"models":[]}
tags-body-closed=true
show-fallback={}
show-body-closed=true
tags-success-count=1
show-success-context=32768
```

<details>
<summary>proof-ollama-provider-models.ts</summary>

```ts
import http from "node:http";
import {
  fetchOllamaModels,
  queryOllamaModelShowInfo,
} from "./extensions/ollama/src/provider-models.ts";

let tagsClosed = false;
let showClosed = false;
let mode: "tags-fail" | "show-fail" | "success" = "tags-fail";

const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {
  if (mode === "tags-fail" && req.url === "/api/tags") {
    res.writeHead(503, { "content-type": "text/plain" });
    res.write("tags unavailable");
    req.socket.on("close", () => {
      tagsClosed = true;
    });
    return;
  }
  if (mode === "show-fail" && req.url === "/api/show") {
    res.writeHead(503, { "content-type": "text/plain" });
    res.write("show unavailable");
    req.socket.on("close", () => {
      showClosed = true;
    });
    return;
  }
  if (mode === "success" && req.url === "/api/tags") {
    res.writeHead(200, { "content-type": "application/json" });
    res.end(JSON.stringify({ models: [{ name: "llama3:8b" }] }));
    return;
  }
  if (mode === "success" && req.url === "/api/show") {
    res.writeHead(200, { "content-type": "application/json" });
    res.end(JSON.stringify({ model_info: { "llama.context_length": 32768 } }));
    return;
  }
  res.writeHead(404, { "content-type": "text/plain" });
  res.end("unexpected");
});

await new Promise<void>((resolve) => server.listen(0, "127.0.0.1", resolve));
const address = server.address();
if (!address || typeof address === "string") {
  throw new Error("expected localhost TCP server address");
}
const baseUrl = `http://127.0.0.1:${address.port}`;

try {
  const tagsFallback = await fetchOllamaModels(baseUrl);
  await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 0));
  console.log(`tags-fallback=${JSON.stringify(tagsFallback)}`);
  console.log(`tags-body-closed=${tagsClosed}`);

  mode = "show-fail";
  const showFallback = await queryOllamaModelShowInfo(baseUrl, "llama3:8b");
  await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 0));
  console.log(`show-fallback=${JSON.stringify(showFallback)}`);
  console.log(`show-body-closed=${showClosed}`);

  mode = "success";
  const tagsSuccess = await fetchOllamaModels(baseUrl);
  const showSuccess = await queryOllamaModelShowInfo(baseUrl, "llama3:8b");
  console.log(`tags-success-count=${tagsSuccess.models.length}`);
  console.log(`show-success-context=${showSuccess.contextWindow}`);
} finally {
  await new Promise<void>((resolve, reject) =>
    server.close((error) => (error ? reject(error) : resolve())),
  );
}
```

</details>

